# Cloudflare Pages / Workers — Redirect Rules
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: Permanent 301 redirects from old domain (creativexlab.online) and
#          non-www new domain (creativextechnology.com) to canonical production
#          domain (https://www.creativextechnology.com).
#
# IMPORTANT DEPLOYMENT NOTES:
# 1. This _redirects file is served by Cloudflare Pages when present in the
#    output/public directory. For Workers-based deployments (vinext), you may
#    instead need to configure Cloudflare Redirect Rules in the Cloudflare
#    dashboard under: Rules → Redirect Rules for each source domain.
# 2. The old domain (creativexlab.online) MUST have its DNS pointing to the
#    same Cloudflare zone or have a separate Cloudflare Redirect Rule configured
#    at the account level before these redirects resolve.
# 3. Do NOT delete or cancel the old domain during the migration.
# 4. Test redirect chains to prevent loops before going live.
# =============================================================================

# Canonical path consolidation: eliminate duplicate ranking / keyword cannibalization
/services/custom-software-development /custom-software-development 301

# Redirect non-www new domain → www (prevents duplicate indexing)
https://creativextechnology.com/* https://www.creativextechnology.com/:splat 301

# Redirect old domain → new www canonical (preserves all URL paths)
https://creativexlab.online/* https://www.creativextechnology.com/:splat 301
https://www.creativexlab.online/* https://www.creativextechnology.com/:splat 301
